{"schema":2,"commit":"27e641962da6315e8da0044dd05195af612c22c6","branch":"fix/nrf91x1-modem-dfu-ipc-masks","base_sha":"3729528d9371f9a634c7b1ef97ef7b8a4b5fb649","message":"nrf91: fix modem firmware update failures from the commander\n\n`nrf91-update-modem-fw` reported \"wait for events timed out\" in cases\nwhere the modem was working fine:\n\n- Any exception raised while verifying was swallowed and turned into a\n  programming attempt. A wrong file path thus showed up as a modem\n  timeout, because the verify had left the modem in its DFU bootloader.\n  Only a firmware mismatch now leads to programming; other errors are\n  reported as they are, and a missing file is reported by parse().\n- The modem stayed in its DFU bootloader after verify/program, including\n  after errors. The device is now reset when the procedure ends.\n- The commander keeps the debug port powered on exit (resume_on_disconnect\n  defaults to False). With debug power still requested, the next modem\n  DFU got no answer, so every second `pyocd cmd` run failed. The command\n  now lets the session resume and power down on exit; the device is reset\n  and running at that point anyway.\n\nTested on an nRF9151 (DAPLink) with mfw-nr+_nrf91x1_1.0.1.zip: verify x4\nin consecutive `pyocd cmd` runs, then -f program + verify (17 s) and a\nfinal verify.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","coding_time_nanos":2690809231241,"totals":{"added_lines":0,"ai_added_lines":0,"human_added_lines":0,"deleted_lines":0,"ai_deleted_lines":0,"human_deleted_lines":0,"files":0},"by_tool":{},"by_gen_type":{"chat":0,"cli":0,"completion":0,"human":0},"files":null,"generated_by":"blamely v1.6.6"}
